      "card_ids": ["C02"],
      "claim": "MBZA, a p-anisoyl amide, showed moderate mouse brain uptake (2.46 %ID/g at 10 min), directly demonstrating that the p-anisoyl amide motif can confer meaningful CNS access; the query retains this same p-anisoyl amide feature.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Aniracetam, a p-anisoyl amide, was detected in rat and human brain and CSF, supporting the ability of p-anisoyl amides to cross the blood-brain barrier.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C11"],
      "claim": "A larger p-anisoyl amide bearing a heteroaromatic piperazine-pyridine substituent showed good brain penetration in NHP PET, indicating that p-anisoyl amide heteroaromatic scaffolds can still access the CNS.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C04"],
      "claim": "Compound 47, an N-methyl amide thiadiazole/pyrimidine analogue with an isopropyl group, had a brain-to-plasma ratio of 0.08 in rat, suggesting that closely related heteroaromatic amides can be efflux-limited; however, it lacks the p-anisoyl amide and contains a more polar thiadiazole, reducing transferability to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "low",
  "decision_summary": "The query is a p-anisoyl N-methyl amide with a thiazole-pyrimidine core. Direct evidence from p-anisoyl amide analogues (MBZA, aniracetam, and a heteroaromatic p-anisoyl amide) supports meaningful CNS access, and the physicochemical profile is consistent with moderate passive permeability. The most similar fail analogue lacks the p-anisoyl amide and contains a more polar thiadiazole, so its poor brain/plasma ratio is less transferable. Overall, evidence leans toward pass, but efflux liability remains uncertain.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma or CSF measurement exists for the exact query scaffold.",
    "P-gp/BCRP efflux substrate status of the query is unknown.",
    "Unbound brain-to-plasma concentration ratio is not available."
  ],
